{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use Spring Data KeyValue (or MapDB-backed implementation) for the off-heap repository used in U1, with Kafka changelog topics as the source of truth for state restoration.",
    "Design a single module-producer acknowledgement (ACK) bus shared by U2 and U3 so offset and state flushing are driven by the same reliability signal, avoiding duplicated plumbing.",
    "For the CoAP source module (U4), adopt the Eclipse Californium framework as the CoAP client stack and expose it as a standard Spring Cloud Stream source.",
    "Model deployment properties (U5, U8) using a typed @ConfigurationProperties POJO hierarchy bound from the YAML manifest so Spring Boot auto-configuration drives the ModuleRunner.",
    "Implement the Diego receptor Java client (U7) on top of Spring's RestTemplate (synchronous) with pluggable authentication (mTLS / basic) to remain compatible with existing Diego cells.",
    "For secured HDFS access (U6), delegate to the standard Hadoop Kerberos login (keytab-based UserGroupInformation.loginUserFromKeytab) so the sqoop runner inherits JVM-wide security context.",
    "Use Spring Boot 3.x (Java 17 baseline, per Spring 6.0) for the Boot-based ModuleRunner (U8) to align with current Spring Framework versions.",
    "Adopt JUnit 5 and Testcontainers (Kafka, Kerberized mini-KDC) for unit and integration tests across all stories."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Estimates assume a single experienced Java/Spring developer with working knowledge of Kafka, Spring Cloud Stream, Hadoop/Sqoop, CoAP, and Spring Boot, but who will need to ramp up briefly on niche areas (off-heap stores, CoAP, Diego receptor protocol).",
    "Existing Spring XD / Spring Cloud Data Flow code base is available and can be extended rather than built from scratch.",
    "Kerberos keytab distribution infrastructure is already in place for U6; only the client-side login code is in scope.",
    "Diego cell endpoint, credentials, and testbed are provided externally for U7; only the Java client library is in scope.",
    "Off-heap memory budget and JVM tuning for U1 are constrained to a single configurable cap; no custom memory allocator is required.",
    "CoAP source module (U4) only needs to support observe-mode subscriptions for a single well-known resource pattern; full CoAP server features are out of scope.",
    "Documentation (U5) refers to the existing deployment manifest schema; the task is filling in/updating the reference docs, not authoring a new docs system.",
    "All upstream dependencies (Kafka brokers, HDFS cluster, Diego cell, CoAP server) are available in the dev/CI environment for testing.",
    "No production hardening, performance benchmarking, or release engineering is included beyond standard unit/integration tests and reference docs.",
    "A standard 8-hour workday is used; overhead for meetings, code reviews, and CI maintenance is included implicitly in per-activity estimates."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and high-level design",
      "activity_description": "Review the 8 user stories, clarify acceptance criteria, produce an architectural sketch (ACK bus, repository abstraction, module wiring, security context propagation), and identify shared components between U2/U3 and U5/U8.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1: Kafka changelog-backed Spring Data repository (off-heap)",
      "activity_description": "Implement a Spring Data repository abstraction whose backing store lives off-heap, with a Kafka changelog topic used to bootstrap and reconcile state. Includes custom repository factory, off-heap adapter, and changelog consumer/producer wiring.",
      "most_likely_effort": 7
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2: Intelligent offset flushing",
      "activity_description": "Add an offset-tracking component that buffers per-partition offsets and only commits them downstream when the module-producer confirms a successful message acknowledgement. Includes commit policy configuration and failure handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3: Intelligent state flushing",
      "activity_description": "Hook the same ACK signal into the off-heap state store so that dirty entries are flushed to the changelog topic only after the corresponding output is acknowledged. Includes dirty-tracking and batched async flush.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4: CoAP source module",
      "activity_description": "Build a new Spring Cloud Stream source module that consumes CoAP notifications (observe mode) using Eclipse Californium, decodes payloads into the internal Message bus format, and exposes configurable resource URI, port, and retry/backoff policies.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5: Properties file documentation",
      "activity_description": "Author/update the reference documentation for the deployment manifest properties, organized by component (modules, transport, security, runtime), with examples and default-value tables.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6: Secured HDFS access for Sqoop jobs",
      "activity_description": "Add Kerberos-aware HDFS configuration to the sqoop job launcher: keytab/principal properties, UGI.loginUserFromKeytab on startup, and propagation of the security context through to the spawned JVM. Includes minimal end-to-end test against a Kerberized HDFS test container.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7: Java receptor client for Diego",
      "activity_description": "Implement a Java client library around Diego's receptor REST API (Tasks, Containers, Cells) using RestTemplate, with pluggable auth, request/response DTOs, and exception mapping. Provide a thin Spring-friendly wrapper for direct DI.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8: Boot-based ModuleRunner and remaining deployment properties",
      "activity_description": "Refactor ModuleRunner into a Spring Boot application with auto-configuration, bind the remaining deployment properties via @ConfigurationProperties, and remove dependency on xd-containers. Includes container-managed lifecycle hooks and graceful shutdown.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Unit testing across all activities",
      "activity_description": "Write JUnit 5 unit tests for each new component: repository adapter, offset/state flushers, CoAP decoder, Sqoop security wiring, receptor client DTOs, and ModuleRunner auto-configuration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing",
      "activity_description": "Compose Testcontainers-based integration tests: Kafka changelog round-trip, ACK-driven offset/state commit, CoAP source against a containerized CoAP server, Sqoop against a Kerberized HDFS mini-cluster, receptor client against a stub Diego endpoint, and Boot-based ModuleRunner end-to-end.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "System testing, bug fixing, and hardening",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end scenarios combining multiple new features, triage failures, and apply targeted fixes plus small refactors uncovered by integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "Documentation finalization and code review polish",
      "activity_description": "Update README, configuration reference, and any inline Javadoc gaps surfaced during review; respond to and incorporate review comments.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 52
  }
}
```

